=== REASONING ===

The §1 pre-flight precondition is met for the first time in this
slice's history (64/64 predecessors). However, the §2 build matrix —
which is the prompt's literal next gate — is red on three Go
sub-tests, the web `npm run lint`, and `npm test -- --run` (see
GATE for full transcripts and exit codes).

These red signals are NOT introduced by this slice. They are drift
created by the predecessor AI feature slices (F0..ML3 and the W1 SPA
wiring), each of which:

  (a) Added new files under `internal/api/` (an ADR-009 frozen
      package), tripping `TestFrozenPackagesNoNewFiles` (67 unauthored
      files vs. baseline). Slice 0008-F7 documented this pattern as
      "pre-existing failure disclosure" and explicitly deferred the
      baseline refresh to "the prior owner of the drift". No subsequent
      slice has paid down that debt; instead each newer slice added more
      AI handlers to the frozen package, growing the gap from 8 (at
      F7) to 67 (now).
  (b) Did not ship a `doc.go` carrying a `// Layer: <name>` declaration,
      tripping `TestEveryInternalPackageHasDocGoWithLayer` (75 packages
      missing — including every per-feature strategy package, every
      provider adapter, and every guard/dispatch package).
  (c) Did not refresh `tools/archmetrics/baseline.json`, dropping the
      internal/ doc.go coverage from a baseline of 100.0% to a current
      58.3% and tripping `TestBaselineHonoured`.
  (d) Introduced lint regressions (24 errors) into pre-existing
      production source under `web/src/features/system/`,
      `web/src/features/telemetry/`, `web/src/hooks/`, and
      `web/src/observability/`. Several are residual
      `eslint-disable` directives that became unused as their
      original `react-hooks/exhaustive-deps` warnings were resolved.
  (e) Introduced vitest regressions (64 failed tests across 11 test
      files), notably:
        - src/features/settings/components/__tests__/AISettings.test.tsx
          throws an unhandled rejection from
          AIProviderSection.tsx:128 (`Cannot read properties of
          undefined (reading 'ok')`) — the slice that wired the
          /settings/ai/validate-config endpoint changed the response
          shape but the component still expects the old `{ ok: true }`
          envelope.
        - src/api/hooks/__tests__/useSignals.test.tsx — pre-existing
          double-prefix regression in /signals/{vid}/available.
        - src/components/charts/__tests__/SmallMultiplesChart.test.tsx
          — chart prop signature drifted relative to the test fixture.
        - src/features/settings/components/{ActiveSessionsSection,TOTPEnrollmentSection}.test.tsx
          — auth-mode probe responses changed shape.
        - src/features/system/components/state-machine/__tests__/StateTimeline*.test.tsx
        - src/features/system/components/status/__tests__/UpdateAvailableCallout.test.tsx
        - src/features/trips/pages/__tests__/TripReplayPage.sync.test.tsx
        - src/features/admin/components/__tests__/RedisDiagnosticEmptyState.test.tsx
        - src/__tests__/lazyRoutes.smoke.test.ts — lazy-route parity
          counter fell out of sync.

Per the prompt's allowed-files list, this slice is NOT permitted to
edit any of the files needed to make the build matrix green:

  - tools/archmetrics/baseline.json     → would fix (a), (b), (c)
  - web/src/features/system/**          → contains 4 of the lint errors
  - web/src/features/telemetry/**       → contains 1 of the lint errors
  - web/src/features/settings/**        → contains the AIProviderSection
                                           shape regression and at least
                                           3 of the failing test files
  - web/src/hooks/**                    → contains 3 of the lint errors
  - web/src/observability/**            → contains 4 of the lint errors
  - any internal/api/* AI handler        → moving each to internal/handler/v1
                                           is the ADR-009-compliant fix
                                           for `TestFrozenPackagesNoNewFiles`

The prompt is unambiguous on the consequence of touching them anyway:

  > NO production source changes. Any production diff in this slice ⇒
  > STATUS=BLOCKED — fix the relevant feature slice instead.

So whether I touch them or do not touch them, the slice is BLOCKED.
The honest path is the latter: do not touch them, run the gate as
written, and record a complete BLOCKED log so the next operator
inherits a clean accounting of the residual debt instead of a
silent partial-fix.

The §3 eval gate, the HX UX project-wide invariants, and (within
the bounds of the existing infrastructure) §1 pre-flight all PASS.
The §4 invariant suite is NOT added by this run for two reasons:

  (i) The new test files described by the prompt (contract_test.go,
      baseline_parity_test.go, egress_interceptor_test.go,
      push_fanout_test.go off-mode extension, ai-off-contract.spec.ts,
      baseline-routes.json) all depend on production helpers that do
      not yet exist in the codebase:
        - `httptest.Do(route)` parser for "METHOD /path" strings,
        - `installProviderHostInterceptor`, `runWorkloadSoak`,
        - `runJobOnce(t, jobName)`, `jobMutationsTouchedRows(t, jobName)`,
        - `loadBaselineRouteList`, `snapshotAllRoutes`, `compareSnapshots`,
        - a Playwright runner config (the existing tests/ai-off-mode.spec.ts
          is a deliberately-inert skeleton that requires RUN_PLAYWRIGHT=1
          AND a configured runner that the repo does not ship).
      Each helper is "production source" by ADR-009's reading and by
      the spirit of the slice's allowed-files list. Adding any of them
      from this slice would itself trip the same "NO production source
      changes" rule that closes (a)–(e) above.

  (ii) Even if the helpers existed, the audit report headline mandated
       by §5 ("Slices completed: 64 / 64 / Build matrix: PASS") cannot
       be honestly stamped while §2 is red. Adding the §4 suite on top
       of a red §2 would either produce a SECOND red gate (false
       progress) or hide the §2 red behind a green §4 (false-green,
       Covenant rule #1).

Forward path to unblock this gate (delegated to the next operator):

  1. Re-open the predecessor slices and pay down the debt they
     deferred:
       a. Move every internal/api/ai_*_handler.go to internal/handler/v1
          (the ADR-009-compliant location for new HTTP surfaces).
       b. Add a `doc.go` with `// Layer: <name>` to each of the 75
          listed packages.
       c. Refresh `tools/archmetrics/baseline.json` once (a) and (b)
          settle, by running:
             go run ./tools/archmetrics > tools/archmetrics/baseline.json
          and committing it alongside (a) + (b).
       d. Fix the 24 lint errors (mostly unused `eslint-disable`
          directives + 2 jsx-a11y label associations + 1 empty
          interface + 2 unused imports).
       e. Fix the AISettings response-shape regression and the 10
          other failing vitest files (each has a small surface-area
          diff in production source).
  2. Re-run THIS slice (9999 final gate). With the build matrix
     green, the §4 invariant suite can be safely added by extending
     this slice's allowed-files list (or, more cleanly, by minting
     a new "9998 invariant-suite" slice that adds the helpers
     listed in §4, then this slice runs verification only).
  3. Tag `phase-50-final-gate` and append the CHANGELOG entry only
     after the green run.

